 "notes": "North is up. E-W names: this half prints W. LIBERTY, WILSTACH, WADE, FLINT, KENNER and HOPKINS without a suffix and CORTLANDT / SEDGEWICK with STREET; the STREET suffix for the others is printed on 22-9R, so all are recorded as '... Street'. CORTLANDT is the 1904 Courtland (Florence); no bracketed old names on this half. Water pipes are drawn as solid lines inside the streets (Liberty, Kenner, Dalton, McLean) and were not used as street lines. McLean Av. (100') is the railroad corridor; Hopkins jogs ~73 px south across it, so there are two T entries at McLean. Cortlandt and Sedgewick end at McLean's continuous east line and resume at Dalton going east. Curran St. (50') runs only from Kenner to Hopkins. Dalton is 50' north of Wade and 60' south; Hopkins is 60' west of Dalton and 80' east of it (south lines aligned), so Dalton/Hopkins and Dalton/Liberty are 4-corner centres. The binding fold runs at about x 5830 and the paper is compressed across it: the Curran-Dalton spacing is ~25 px shorter here than on 22-9R. Gutter overlap with 22-9R: Curran/Kenner, Curran/Hopkins and the eight Dalton intersections (Liberty to Hopkins)."
